# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# There was no such file, and it mattered more than it looks: `COPY frontend/ ./` in the
# frontend image was copying the host's node_modules in on top of the one the image had just
# installed. With npm that was merely slow -- real directories landing on real directories.
# With pnpm the host tree is a farm of symlinks into a store that does not exist inside the
# container, so the build died on a missing tsc that was right there a layer earlier.

**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.git
.github

# Build output and scratch from the native engine and its tooling.
Engine/x64
CLI/x64
GUI/x64
**/build
**/*.o
**/*.obj

# Test artefacts: screenshots and reports are written by the suites, never read by an image.
frontend/shots
frontend/test-results
**/*.log
